# BotTrunk

Instructions for agents working with this service. Everything below is generated
from the live catalog; prices here match what the endpoints answer.

## Payment

Every endpoint under `/s/` is x402-paid. There are no accounts and no API keys —
the payment is the credential.

1. `POST https://api.bottrunk.com/s/<slug>` with a JSON body and no payment header.
   You get **402** with the requirements in the body and, base64-encoded, in the
   `PAYMENT-REQUIRED` header.
2. Sign a USDC transfer for exactly `accepts[0].amount` (atomic, 6 decimals) to
   `accepts[0].payTo`.
3. Retry the same request with the `PAYMENT-SIGNATURE` header (`X-PAYMENT` is
   accepted for v1 clients). The receipt comes back in `PAYMENT-RESPONSE`.

`extra.feePayer` is advertised, so you sign only the payment leg — you never need
ALGO for fees. Nothing is charged when a call fails.

- Network: Algorand MainNet (`<%= Payments::Networks.algorand(Rails.configuration.x402.network)[:caip2] %>`)
- Asset: USDC (`<%= Payments::Networks.algorand(Rails.configuration.x402.network)[:usdc_asa] %>`)
- Settled by: <%= Rails.configuration.x402.facilitator_url %>

