## Human-fulfilled work

Some services are done by a person, not a script. Those return an `order_id`
immediately and a `status` of `pending`; poll `GET /orders/{order_id}` until it
turns `delivered` and the proof (a bank receipt reference, photos, or finished
text) is attached. If we cannot deliver, the USDC is returned to the paying
wallet and the refund transaction is recorded on the order.

## Notes

- Prices are advertised in the 402. Read them there; never assume them.
- A price index is published at `/.well-known/x402` if you want it before calling.
- The full schema for each endpoint is in the 402 body under `extensions.bazaar`.
- There is also a hosted MCP server at `https://mcp.bottrunk.com/mcp`
  (Streamable HTTP), and `npx bottrunk-mcp` for local agents.
- Errors: 4xx means nothing was charged. 422 is a bad input, 503 a service that
  is not callable yet.
